      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What permissions are available?",
      "Anchor": "what-permissions-are-available",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What permissions are available?"
      ],
      "Text": "In addition to these permissions, members must have the appropriate roles as defined in Company Page Roles and Ad Account Roles to act on or read data from a given Company Page or Ad Account. See How Do I Know What Roles a Member Has to determine which roles an authenticated member has through the API.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What permissions are available?",
      "Anchor": "what-permissions-are-available",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What permissions are available?"
      ],
      "Text": "Note",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "What permissions are available?",
      "Anchor": "what-permissions-are-available",
      "SectionPath": [
        "What permissions are available?"
      ],
      "Text": "Access to Advertising API is a mandatory requirement for applying to Matched Audiences API, Audience Insights API and Media Planning API.\nAudience Insights API does not require any additional member permission to be passed in OAuth2 scope for member consent.\nFor restricted APIs, LinkedIn evaluates applications based on partnership fit and access criteria. Restricted APIs are evaluated on a case-by-case basis with no fixed timeline \u2014 contact Developer Support for status updates.\nRefer to the list in the API Products and Permissions table.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How to Upgrade your Access Tier",
      "Anchor": "how-to-upgrade-your-access-tier",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Upgrade your Access Tier"
      ],
      "Text": "The Advertising API and Community Management API each have two access tiers with different access criteria. All applications start with Development tier. You must apply separately to upgrade to the Standard tier.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
    {
      "Kind": "text",
      "Section": "How to Upgrade your Access Tier",
      "Anchor": "how-to-upgrade-your-access-tier",
      "SectionPath": [
        "How to Upgrade your Access Tier"
      ],
      "Text": "Advertising API: Development tier is designed to build end-to-end workflows and supports read-only access for unlimited ad accounts and edit capabilities for up to five (5) Ad Accounts. Standard tier is designed to support campaign management solutions including edit capabilities for unlimited ad accounts.\nCommunity Management API: Development tier is designed to build and test integrations with API call restrictions. You must complete your integration and testing within twelve months of receiving the API access. Standard tier is designed for live production with no restrictions.",
      "Headers": [],
      "Rows": []
    },
